        " : «إِذَا أَرَدْتَ أَنْ تَطُوفَ عَنْ أَحَدٍ مِنْ إِخْوَانِكَ فَائْتِ اَلْحَجَرَ اَلْأَسْوَدَ وَ قُلْ بِسْمِ اَللَّهِ اَللَّهُمَّ تَقَبَّلْ مِنْ فُلاَنٍ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2829 - It is narrated from Muawiyah ibn Ammar, from Abu Abdullah (as), that he said:\n\"If you wish to perform Tawaf on behalf of one of your brothers, go to the Black Stone and say,\n'In the name of Allah (swt), O Allah (swt), accept this on behalf of [the name of the person].'\""
        ]
      }
